🔹 Program 14: Object Slicing Demonstration

📌 Description

This program demonstrates object slicing.

When a derived object is passed by value to a function expecting a base object, only the base-class portion is copied.

When the same object is passed by reference, the complete derived object is preserved and virtual function dispatch works correctly.

🎯 Concept Used

Object Slicing and Polymorphism Using References

💡 Key Point

Passing a polymorphic object by "Base" value can cause object slicing. Using a reference or pointer preserves the derived object.
